tsart - Automated Refactoring Tools, for Typescript 7.0.2
--------------------

Neovim AST selection
--------------------

`tsart nvim` runs a Neovim remote-plugin host. It provides `:TsartSelectAST`,
which parses the current buffer (including unsaved edits) and reports the AST
token under the cursor with its TypeScript byte range. `:TsartHighlightAST`
highlights that token in the buffer; `:TsartClearASTHighlight` removes it.

Build and install the host first:

```sh
make install
```

Then register it from your Neovim config. The install target writes the binary
to `~/.config/tsart/tsart`, so the host does not accidentally use an older
`tsart` found elsewhere on `PATH`:

```vim
let s:tsart_binary = expand('~/.config/tsart/tsart')
function! s:RequireTsart(host) abort
  return jobstart([s:tsart_binary, 'nvim'], {'rpc': v:true})
endfunction
call remote#host#Register('tsart', 'x', function('s:RequireTsart'))
call remote#host#RegisterPlugin('tsart', '0', [
   {'type': 'command', 'name': 'TsartSelectAST', 'sync': 1,
    'opts': {'eval': '{''FileName'': expand(''%:p''), ''Text'': join(getline(1, ''$''), "\\n"), ''Line'': line(''.''), ''Column'': col(''.'') - 1}'}},
   {'type': 'command', 'name': 'TsartHighlightAST', 'sync': 1,
    'opts': {'eval': '{''FileName'': expand(''%:p''), ''Text'': join(getline(1, ''$''), "\\n"), ''Line'': line(''.''), ''Column'': col(''.'') - 1}'}},
   {'type': 'command', 'name': 'TsartClearASTHighlight', 'sync': 1, 'opts': {}},
   {'type': 'command', 'name': 'TsartAnnotateSelection', 'sync': 1,
    'opts': {'nargs': '+', 'range': '', 'eval': '{''Text'': join(getline(1, ''$''), "\\n"), ''StartLine'': line("''<"), ''StartColumn'': col("''<"), ''EndLine'': line("''>"), ''EndColumn'': col("''>"), ''Mode'': visualmode()}'}},
   ])
```

Open a TypeScript buffer, put the cursor on a symbol, then run
`:TsartHighlightAST`. The highlight uses Neovim's `Visual` highlight group,
so it follows your colorscheme.

Visual annotations
------------------

Select text in Visual or Visual-line mode, then run `:TsartAnnotateSelection`
followed by your comment, for example `:TsartAnnotateSelection rename this
before export`. tsart highlights the selected text and shows the comment beside
it. The annotation is an extmark, so it follows the selected text as the
buffer is edited. Blockwise selections are not supported.
